id: pm-rust-1ps2
title: "release-check passes locally and fails in CI whenever CHANGELOG_DATE is overridden, because this repository has no git tags to date releases from"
description: "The justfile hardcodes CHANGELOG_DATE 2026-08-07 and CI runs just release-check with no override, so the committed CHANGELOG.md must be generated at that exact date. This repository has no git tags at all, so --all-release-tags derives no tag windows and every heading is dated purely by --date."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog,clock-dependence,release-gate
created_at: "2026-08-16T01:37:49.364Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T23:03:49.403Z"
deadline: "2026-08-31T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T16:18:41.960Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T16:18:41.960Z"
claim_principal: ox-alpha
author: claude-code
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Generating the changelog in a working copy and verifying it in CI cannot disagree; either the date is derived from a real tag, or an overridden CHANGELOG_DATE cannot silently produce a committed file that CI rejects"
resolution: "changelog-check/release-check no longer forward CHANGELOG_DATE; they verify the canonical pinned justfile constant, which the release workflow rewrites before generating and commits atomically. The changelog toolchain pins both pm-changelog@2026.8.6 and @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.6 exactly, eliminating silent truncation under floating SDK reads."
expected_result: Generating the changelog in a working copy and verifying it in CI cannot disagree regardless of date overrides or SDK resolution.
actual_result: Clean-clone cold-npx-cache run of just changelog-check returns rc=0 (previously failed in CI); a hostile CHANGELOG_DATE override is ignored by verification; a committed override-generated file now fails locally with rc=1 matching CI. 5 new contract tests lock both guarantees.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rust-u4al,related,"2026-08-16T01:37:49.364Z",claude-code,"cli:create:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T01:37:49.364Z",claude-code,"The justfile already documents the nested-just override problem for changelog-check. That comment addresses a different failure: it makes a release run verify against the date it generated with. It does not address a contributor overriding the date outside a release, which is what happened here."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T01:37:49.364Z",claude-code,"Related fleet-wide pattern: pm-changelog clock dependence has bitten this fleet twice before, once through timezone handling and once through an untagged today-fallback."
  "2026-08-21T16:02:00.937Z",ox-alpha,"Diagnosis confirmed: the divergence channel is the explicit CHANGELOG_DATE forwarding in changelog-check/release-check (nested just), so a contributor override verified a different file than CI's default. Fix design: the check boundary now always verifies against the canonical pinned justfile constant (override ignored there); generation recipes keep honoring the override; the release workflow rewrites the constant to the tag-derived release date BEFORE generating and commits the justfile atomically with CHANGELOG.md. A runtime-clock default was rejected deliberately: with zero tags it would churn the heading date daily and fail the gate every day after the first."
  "2026-08-21T23:03:49.382Z","harness:ox-alpha","Review follow-up (CodeRabbit PR #20): the author_source=asserted events in lines 2-6 were required because the pi harness session-file identity resolver failed (agent_provenance_outcomes.model: resolver_failed), so identity was asserted from the operator environment; this update is written with automatic harness-derived identity instead. Closure evidence completed per review: links .github/workflows/ci.yml (PM CLI pin change) and records all six new contract guards - changelog_toolchain_pins_the_sdk_exactly and ci_pm_cli_pin_is_single_and_current are now linked alongside the four originally listed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T01:37:49.364Z",claude-code,"A gate whose verdict changes with no change to its inputs is measuring the clock. Here the input is a hardcoded date constant rather than the wall clock, but the effect on a contributor is identical."
